  "consumerReconciliation": [
    "Python 3.11 target, pyright/mypy/ty, thin generated metadata/models and shared runtime validation are consistent; explicit update kwargs replace dictionary-shaped bulk updates.",
    "Bounded DSL forms, aggregates, explicit null-safe comparisons and to-one joins have named gates. Owner-set typing refuses repeated/self/ambiguous joins until an alias surface qualifies; same-owner comparison avoids a foreign Column[Any,T] escape.",
    "Async operations, streams, validation, timeout settlement and typed created/changed result views are specified without claiming the existing spike proves them. Streaming delivers complete pages and explicit failure, with cleanup/quarantine and compatible host-transaction admission.",
    "Schema-neutral catalogs bind runtime resolution to host-supplied independent expectations. Cache reuse cannot cache authority or dependency fences; DDL invalidation proof or fresh verification is required. Privilege reports include runtime metadata/admission/reconciliation work and unresolved host obligations.",
    "Praxis Lakebase/Postgres reads can proceed in parallel with Truss. Shared semantics and Weft owner artifacts precede dependent catalogs; raw bulk follows native action qualification. Existing browser SQL-to-actions work remains independent and retains its frozen source cohort."
  ],
  "boundedChoicesNotBlockers": [
    "roles/1 refuses service targets until a separate service authorization profile is defined and qualified.",
    "Repeated/self/ambiguous joins and unqualified native frame or commit receipt mechanisms refuse instead of silently broadening support.",
    "Asynchronous filtered search permits explicit partial results; complete current top-k requires a qualified coherent index/table snapshot.",
    "Truss lexical exactness, publication location/release cadence and implementation spending ceiling remain explicit owner decisions."
  ],
  "remainingQualificationGates": [
    "Weft-owned versioned command/search artifact interfaces, structural digest projection, capture boundary and golden corpus; no local SQL lowering or stripped-SQL substitute.",
    "Actual Python 3.11 interpreter execution plus generated ABI and expanded DSL/model/result forms on all three pinned checkers, including optional joins and narrowed read-only result views.",
    "Independent native witnesses per backend/version for schema resolution/cache invalidation, privileges, human-role correspondence, transitive dependency admission/fencing, atomic result markers, uniqueness/concurrency, receipts, timeout/cancellation and original-scope reconciliation.",
    "Truss exact issued revision, rich original outcomes, protected controls/recovery and native/local profile adoption; Ashlar immutable publication/resolver/fencing/ACK obligations with original witnesses.",
    "New umf.access model content and merged producer sources require a new separately prepared and admitted source cohort. Existing browser component evidence does not qualify this SDK."
  ],
